WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:02.068 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Hi, hi.

00:00:02.068 --> 00:00:03.903 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Hey. Hi. Hello.

00:00:03.903 --> 00:00:05.638 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:05.638 --> 00:00:10.543 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm -- I'm sorry if I seem
a little bit --

00:00:10.543 --> 00:00:13.480 align:start size:94% position:6%
a little bit
out of it right now.

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:18.151 line:92%
I -- I got my lab results back.

00:00:18.151 --> 00:00:22.455 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, uh, just as
every doctor suspected,

00:00:22.455 --> 00:00:24.557 size:75% position:38% line:92%
I'm simply too much.

00:00:24.557 --> 00:00:28.528 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:28.528 --> 00:00:35.435 align:start size:94% position:6%
I -- I come to you as
a carefree, platinum blond.

00:00:35.435 --> 00:00:38.138 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:38.138 --> 00:00:41.775
But I haven't always been
a carefree, platinum blond.

00:00:41.775 --> 00:00:42.742 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:42.742 --> 00:00:48.314 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was actually born
and raised as a brunette.

00:00:48.314 --> 00:00:49.716 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:49.716 --> 00:00:53.586 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I've been a platinum blond
for about five years now,

00:00:53.586 --> 00:00:59.325 align:start size:94% position:6%
except for a month-long period
somewhere in the middle,

00:00:59.325 --> 00:01:04.964
where I had a suspicious mole
on my back that I had to get

00:01:04.964 --> 00:01:07.600 size:78% position:39% line:92%
removed and biopsied.

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:13.306 align:start size:94% position:6%
For that period, I went back
to being a brunette

00:01:13.306 --> 00:01:16.576 line:92%
because I thought, "No no.

00:01:16.576 --> 00:01:19.846 align:start size:94% position:6%
Blond Juilo
can't deal with that."

00:01:19.846 --> 00:01:23.216 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:23.216 --> 00:01:26.553 align:start size:94% position:6%
That sounds like a job
for a brunette.

00:01:26.553 --> 00:01:29.189 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:29.189 --> 00:01:36.663 align:start size:94% position:6%
I -- I just updated
the software on my iPhone.

00:01:36.663 --> 00:01:37.564 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Sighs ]

00:01:37.564 --> 00:01:38.431 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:38.431 --> 00:01:42.702
And I was mortified to find out
that when you update

00:01:42.702 --> 00:01:49.776 align:start size:94% position:6%
your software, what used to be
the shooting star emoji

00:01:49.776 --> 00:01:52.345 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
becomes a meteor.

00:01:52.345 --> 00:01:54.380 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:54.380 --> 00:02:03.890
Now, I don't know if Apple knows
that the difference

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:05.658 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
is monumental.

00:02:05.658 --> 00:02:07.193 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:07.193 --> 00:02:09.295 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because, of course,
a shooting star emoji

00:02:09.295 --> 00:02:10.830 align:start size:94% position:6%
was this gorgeous stroke
of iridescence.

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:14.234
It'd go from a very deep blue
to a very soothing baby blue

00:02:14.234 --> 00:02:15.735 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
to, like, ah!

00:02:15.735 --> 00:02:18.404 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:18.404 --> 00:02:25.011
The meteor, on the other hand,
is this aggressive orange ball

00:02:25.011 --> 00:02:25.879 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
of fire.

00:02:25.879 --> 00:02:26.412 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:26.412 --> 00:02:30.550 align:start size:94% position:6%
So for the longest time,
I thought I was being flirty

00:02:30.550 --> 00:02:34.487 align:start size:94% position:6%
when really,
I was being a psychopath.

00:02:34.487 --> 00:02:37.223 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:37.223 --> 00:02:39.692 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'd get text messages being
like, "Hey, Julio.

00:02:39.692 --> 00:02:42.262
Will I see you later?"
And I'd be like, "I don't know.

00:02:42.262 --> 00:02:43.530 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Maybe." Ah!

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:45.031 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.031 --> 00:02:48.268 align:start size:94% position:6%
When really I was going,
"Maybe!"

00:02:48.268 --> 00:02:52.572 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:52.572 --> 00:02:55.775 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I --

00:02:55.775 --> 00:02:59.045 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:59.045 --> 00:03:03.683
I -- I brought this up
to the genius at the Mac store.

00:03:03.683 --> 00:03:05.285 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:05.285 --> 00:03:09.822
And he said, "Sir, I have
to move on with my life."

00:03:09.822 --> 00:03:11.791 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:11.791 --> 00:03:18.097
As you can probably tell by now,
my favorite color is clear,

00:03:18.097 --> 00:03:21.267 line:92%
followed closely by shiny.

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:21.901 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Light laughter ]

00:03:21.901 --> 00:03:26.272
I first remember the first time
I ever fell in love

00:03:26.272 --> 00:03:27.006 size:78% position:39% line:92%
with the color clear.

00:03:27.006 --> 00:03:31.978
I was a little boy, and I saw
Cinderella's pretty little feet

00:03:31.978 --> 00:03:34.514 line:92%
going into that glass slipper.

00:03:34.514 --> 00:03:40.420 align:start size:94% position:6%
When I saw that, I was like,
"What is that?

00:03:40.420 --> 00:03:41.654 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:41.654 --> 00:03:44.657 size:81% position:41% line:92%
Mother, let's rewind."

00:03:44.657 --> 00:03:46.960 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:48.695 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she was like,
"Rewind to what?"

00:03:48.695 --> 00:03:51.297 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm like,
"You know to what.

00:03:51.297 --> 00:03:52.498 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:52.498 --> 00:03:54.534 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
To the shoe."

00:03:54.534 --> 00:03:55.535 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Light laughter ]

00:03:55.535 --> 00:03:59.505 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, a lot keeps me up
at night these days.

00:03:59.505 --> 00:04:01.074 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:01.074 --> 00:04:04.043 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
But -- okay.

00:04:04.043 --> 00:04:08.314 align:start size:94% position:6%
Remember that scene in
"Cinderella" where she has to

00:04:08.314 --> 00:04:12.318 size:78% position:39%
rush out of the ball,
and she leaves behind

00:04:12.318 --> 00:04:13.653 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
that glass slipper?

00:04:13.653 --> 00:04:18.825
The prince finds the shoe, and
this is all has has left of her.

00:04:18.825 --> 00:04:23.062
But then, presumably, there's
a scene where the prince goes

00:04:23.062 --> 00:04:26.566 align:start size:94% position:6%
to his subjects and he goes,
"Have every maiden

00:04:26.566 --> 00:04:32.338
in the kingdom try this on
until you find the girl I met

00:04:32.338 --> 00:04:33.940 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
at the ball."

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:38.077 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I bet there were like,
"Or...

00:04:38.077 --> 00:04:39.212 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:39.212 --> 00:04:43.783 align:start size:94% position:6%
...you could just come with us
and look at their faces."

00:04:43.783 --> 00:04:46.719 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:46.719 --> 00:04:55.695 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:55.695 --> 00:04:58.931
And he was probably like,
"But who would we use the shoe?"

00:04:58.931 --> 00:05:01.000 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:04.337
You know, just because you have
a tool doesn't mean that

00:05:04.337 --> 00:05:05.571 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
you have to use it.

00:05:05.571 --> 00:05:08.474 align:start size:94% position:6%
Okay, unless there's
any questions, thank you all.

00:05:08.474 --> 00:05:11.878 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:11.878 --> 00:05:16.549 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Band plays ]

00:05:16.549 --> 00:05:18.384 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Julio Torres!

00:05:18.384 --> 00:05:23.222 align:start size:94% position:6%
